 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Use",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Made for the control FET position of synchronous buck point-of-load converters in networking, telecom and computing systems. Qg, Qgd and RDS(on) are kept low to reduce loss in power conversion."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Threshold is 1.1 to 1.9 V at 250 µA. On-resistance is specified at two drive levels with 10 A flowing: 9.3 mΩ max at 4.5 V and 6.9 mΩ max at 10 V. Charging the gate to 4.5 V takes 7.9 nC typical and to 10 V 17.2 nC typical, from a 15 V drain with 10 A. Internal series gate resistance is 1.8 Ω typical, 3.6 Ω max. Figure 7 shows on-resistance climbing steeply once VGS falls below about 4 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current limits",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The package caps continuous drain current at 25 A; the silicon alone would carry 59 A at a 25 °C case. On a 1 in² copper pad with 40 °C/W junction-to-ambient the continuous rating is 16 A and dissipation 3.1 W. Figure 12 holds 25 A up to roughly 125 °C case and falls to zero at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "On-resistance rises with case temperature: normalized to 25 °C it is about 0.7 at −55 °C and about 1.7 at 150 °C. Threshold falls from about 1.8 V at −55 °C to about 0.9 V at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Avalanche",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Single-pulse avalanche energy is 23 mJ at 22 A peak in a 0.1 mH inductor. Figure 11 gives peak avalanche current against time in avalanche for starting temperatures of 25 °C and 125 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The body diode drops 0.8 V typical, 1.0 V max, at 10 A. Reverse recovery at 300 A/µs from 10 A into 15 V takes 6.8 ns with 6.5 nC of charge."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Junction to case is at most 3.8 °C/W. Junction to ambient is at most 50 °C/W with 1 in² of 2 oz copper under the drain and 140 °C/W with only the minimum pad; RθJA is set by the user's board."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Handling",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "Built-in ESD protection is limited. Keep the leads shorted together, or the part in conductive foam, while it is stored or handled, to protect the MOS gate from static."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Moisture and reflow",
   "page": 11,
   "text": "MSL 1 at 260 °C peak reflow, unlimited floor life. Lead finish is tin (SN)."
  }
 ],
